All around you are the inner workings of Casimirage, taking the form of 
enormous mechanical devices.  A stack of instructions is being continually fed
from Ol'en through the core to what appears to be a small console in the 
corner, displaying rapidly changing scenery as Ol'en alters itself. A penguin
wearing a red fedora sits on a platform high above, silently overseeing the 
process. He holds a socket wrench and guards what appears to be the root of a
massive tree. A sign above the penguin reads: "Colonel Linuz". A conveyor belt
transports the decomposed garbage from Ol'en to a giant vat of boiling liquid
where it appears to be recycled, for from this liquid, a crane occasionally 
lifts a new formless object, and drops it through one of many chutes that line
the walls. In the center of all of this is a metal core with "CISTOMS" embossed
in its surface. On this core upon which everything is built is a lever, above
which is printed, "Emergency Halt." You decide that pulling this lever would be
a colossally bad idea, and refrain.
